 "about": "PAT16 of OpenNeuro ds001226 (CC0), two-tensor UKF, the case library's stored result (Contents/data/tractcloud/cases/PAT16.json, 2026-10-01). The regression test (cases.regression.test.ts) reruns the case and compares; a deliberate change that moves these numbers rewrites this file in the same commit, with the reason. Rewritten 2026-10-01 night: the seed's FA computed as the original UKFTractography does for the simple model (the mean of the two minor eigenvalues; ukf.ts), which tracks fewer seeds -- from the same seeds the port now tracks the same seeds as the original (838 fibers each). Rewritten 2026-10-02: whole-brain seeds start only inside the brain (DIPY's median_otsu mask; the head mask put a third of them in the scalp), 16,000 of them (25,000 before; about the same count of streamlines); tracking still runs inside the head mask (median_otsu cuts the top of the brain); and the tracker's constraint projection is exact (the card's too). Judged against the noise floors (agreement.ts), the near-tumor list changed as much as a new seed draw changes it. Rewritten 2026-10-03: the names come from RapidParc (rapidparc/, Ron: Albula switches to it, as Mike Halle's tractline did) instead of TractCloud -- same streamlines (10,828), naming 0.7 s instead of 2.8 s; 27 named tracts near the tumor instead of 30: RapidParc puts more streamlines into the large tracts (thalamo-frontal 196 against 113, inferior longitudinal fasciculus 78 against 31), drops four superficial and two corona radiata/callosal groups TractCloud listed with few streamlines, and adds corpus callosum 6 and the left frontal corona radiata. Rewritten 2026-10-03: Rule 2 of the distortion correction (distortion.ts): the field estimated together with the PA scan's movement between the two scans, alpha 500 (validation step 4; Ron, 2026-10-03: \"Build\"). Rewritten 2026-10-04: Tracking rule 2 (tracking-rules.ts; Ron, 2026-10-03: 'please follow Mike's lead'): plain two-tensor UKF, the shell nearest b = 3000, every brain voxel a seed, seed FA 0.1, stop at FA 0.08 or mean signal 0.06, a point every 1.8 mm, inside the brain mask -- Mike Halle's tractline's, the ORG atlas's. Rewritten 2026-10-04: Aligned to the T1 (registration.ts, Ron 2026-10-03: 'Number three, go'): the corrected b = 0 aligned rigidly to the case's T1 on normalized gradient fields (as Mike Halle's tractline), and the scan read once onto the T1's axes through the move and the distortion field; tracked by tracking rule 2. Rewritten 2026-10-03: After the critic (qa/2026-10-03-dmri-rule2-registration.md): the T1-aligned grid keeps the scan's voxel volume and covers the brain plus a margin; the scan's edge voxels are kept. Rewritten 2026-10-04: tracking rule 3 is the default (2026-10-04): the brain from SynthStrip on the T1 Rewritten 2026-10-04: rule 3 after the critic's round (2026-10-04): the brain only where the scan has data, a fixed 4-voxel box margin Rewritten 2026-10-04: tracking rule 4 is the default (2026-10-04 evening): rule 3 without the fluid; within6 added Rewritten 2026-10-04: rule 3 with the outside-the-brain naming (outside-brain.ts) and the 6 mm list (2026-10-04 evening) Rewritten 2026-10-04: rule 3, the 6 mm list with the gray band; the outside-the-brain naming built but off (2026-10-04 night) Rewritten 2026-10-04: rule 3, the 6 mm list with the gray band, the outside-the-brain test off (recorded as 0); after the critic's round on the build (2026-10-04 night) Rewritten 2026-10-05: head-movement correction (motion rule 1) became the default, albula-diffusion 78055ef: each image put back where the head was before the fit",
